add(evidence,'p','The event-history matcher suggests exact normalized title matches and explicitly linked records. A title match is a candidate, not proof of the same person or situation. You must confirm a saved comparison before reusing it. The app copies its original expectations, never treats an unchosen option as observed, and then uses the existing checked feeling and resource calibration in the main tradeoff score. Happiness ratings are reused only when the saved scale matches your current scale.');
add(evidence,'p','Calendar check-ins are separate retrospective observations: “worth it / mixed / not worth it,” optional actual minutes, and effort. No response is not a negative response. Only attended, completed events with valid timestamps count. For repeated exact-title activities, the displayed worth-it tendency is (worth-it count + 1) / (all rated events + 3), a Dirichlet(1,1,1) smoothed three-category estimate. It appears only after three reports; this threshold and prior are product assumptions. It is not a happiness forecast, causal effect, or validated personal prediction, and it does not automatically become a score criterion. Retrospective calendar observations are not used to backfill pre-decision forecasts or pass chronological accuracy checks.');
